<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wilhelmshaven</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wilhelmshaven is a port city on the Jade Bight on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> as a naval base on land bought from Oldenburg in 1853 and named after King William I in 1869, it became the main North Sea base of the German navy. It passed to Oldenburg in 1937 and remains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s largest naval base.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wilhelmshaven.jpg" alt="Wilhelmshaven" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martina Nolte · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2012-05-28_Fotoflug_Cuxhaven_Wilhelmshaven_DSC_3909.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
